<h2>Segment 307 &mdash; actual objects and visual perception</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s307S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w1">skyon</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w2">med</span> de, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307school"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307school_dbu">dbu</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307school_sems">sems</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307two">gnyis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w5">don</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w6">shes</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w7">yod</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w8">med</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w9">mtshungs</span> mi mtshungs <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w10">dpyod</span> pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w11">skabs</span> yin pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w12">phyir</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w13">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w14">yi dvags</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w15"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w16">mig</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w17">shes</span></span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w18"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w19">chu</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w20">klung</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w21"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w22">rnag</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w23">khrag</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w24">tu</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w25">snang</span> ba&#x27;i tshe na, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w26">de ltar</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w27">snang</span> ba&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w28"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w29">mig</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w30">shes</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w31">tshad ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w32">ma</span> yin pa <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w33">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w34"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w35">chu</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w36">klung</span></span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s307look_at">la</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w37">bltas</span> pa de&#x27;i tshe na, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w38"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w39">rnag</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w40">khrag</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w41">dngos gnas pa</span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s307w42">zhig</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w43">yod pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w44">mi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w45">&#x27;gal ba</span>&#x27;i phyir</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s307S">And yet there is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w2">no</span> such <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w1">problem</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w12">for</span> this quotation appears in the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w11">section</span> where we are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w10">examining</span> the question of whether, in the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307school">schools of the <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307school_dbu">Middle Way</span> and the <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307school_sems">Mind-Only</span></span>, an <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w5">object</span> and the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w6">perception</span> of it must be <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w9">equivalent</span> in either both <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w7">existing</span> or both <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w8">not existing</span>. <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w13">Moreover</span>, there is another fact about this situation, where the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w18"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w20">stream</span> of <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w19">water</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w25">appears</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w24">as</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w21"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w22">pus</span> and <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w23">blood</span></span> to the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w15"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w16">visual</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w17">consciousness</span></span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w14">craving spirit</span>. It is <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w44">no</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w45">inconsistency</span> to say that the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w28"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w29">visual</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w30">consciousness</span></span> that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w27">sees</span> things <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w26">this way</span> is <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w32">not</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w31">valid perception</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w33">and</span> to say at the same time that--when the craving spirit <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w37">looks</span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s307look_at">at</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w34"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w36">stream</span> of <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w35">water</span></span>--there does <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w43">exist</span> there <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w41">actual</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307w38"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w39">pus</span> and <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s307w40">blood</span></span>.<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s307two"><span class="nul">Two is grammatically fused into the explicit two-school enumeration; no separately alignable English numeral is present. Both later refers to the object/perception pair, not this count.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s307w42"><span class="nul">Indefinite zhig has no separate English exponent in actual pus and blood; English contains no a/some for this noun phrase.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex (gpt-6-astra), reconciling independent Tibetan-first and English-first proposals. Dbu sems is the established abbreviated two-school expression; gnyis is fused into the explicit enumeration and has no separate numeral. The first snang is linked to the stream's appears, not the earlier quotation appears; the second snang is GMR's sees from the viewpoint of the visual consciousness, with supplied things unwrapped. The complete tshad ma ma yin predicate denies a valid perception; tshad ma owns valid perception and standalone negator ma owns not, while is a stays unwrapped. Yod/med express existing/not existing; mi mtshungs is the distributed negative alternative of the equivalence question and stays omitted. Each stream, pus/blood and visual-consciousness occurrence is distinct; the single yi dvags owns only the first craving spirit. Zhig has no separate indefinite exponent. Temporal, copular and remaining causal framing are omitted where distributed. Both complete source columns and all GMR wording remain verbatim; no master gloss is changed.</div>
